\b\fs32 Kiterank – Google Ads API Design Documentation\b0\fs24
\par\par

\b Overview\b0
\par
Kiterank is a SaaS dashboard platform built for small and medium-sized businesses. It aggregates data from Google Business Profile, Google Search Console, and Google Ads into a single interface, helping business owners monitor performance, identify wasted spend, and make data-driven decisions without needing marketing expertise.
\par\par

\b How Kiterank Uses the Google Ads API\b0
\par
Kiterank uses the Google Ads API to retrieve campaign and keyword performance data on behalf of connected client accounts. Specifically, the application:
\par\par
1. Lists accessible customer accounts linked to the authenticated user via \i CustomerService.ListAccessibleCustomers\i0
\par
2. Retrieves campaign-level metrics (spend, clicks, impressions, conversions) via GAQL queries on the \i campaign\i0  resource
\par
3. Retrieves keyword-level metrics (spend, clicks, conversions, match type) via GAQL queries on the \i keyword_view\i0  resource
\par
4. Identifies "wasted" keywords — those with spend but zero conversions — and surfaces them to the user with a recommendation to pause
\par\par

\b Data Flow\b0
\par
- The business owner connects their Google account via OAuth 2.0 (scope: \i https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\i0 )
\par
- Kiterank stores the refresh token securely in a PostgreSQL database (Supabase)
\par
- A daily automated sync fetches the latest 30-day campaign and keyword data
\par
- The user can also trigger a manual sync from the dashboard
\par
- All data is scoped to the connected company and is not shared across accounts
\par\par

\b Access Pattern\b0
\par
- One Google Ads account per connected business client
\par
- Read-only access to campaign and keyword metrics
\par
- No write operations (no creating, modifying, or deleting campaigns or keywords)
\par
- Data is fetched and cached in our database; API calls are made once per day per account
\par\par

\b Technical Stack\b0
\par
- Frontend/Backend: Next.js (TypeScript)
\par
- Database: PostgreSQL via Supabase
\par
- Hosting: Vercel
\par
- Google Ads API version: v19+
\par
- Authentication: OAuth 2.0 with offline access (refresh tokens)
